{
  "title": "Participles and infinitives",
  "note": "A participle is a verbal adjective: λύων, λύουσα, λῦον, 'loosing'. It agrees with its noun, and with the article it means 'the one who': ὁ πιστεύων, 'the one who believes'. The present participle shows ongoing action; the aorist (λύσας, 'having loosed') a single or earlier one. The participle of εἰμί is ὤν, οὖσα, ὄν. The infinitive is a verbal noun: λύειν, λῦσαι, εἶναι.",
